{title: Line of Perez}
{subtitle: 1 Chronicles 2:4–5; Ruth 4:18–20; Matthew 1:3–4; Luke 3:32–33}
{key: Em}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Em] | [Em] | [Em] | [Em] |
| [Em] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Tamar bore Perez and Zerah
Judah had five [Am7]sons in all
Sons of Perez [Em]are Hezron
And Hamul stands beside him tall
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]From Perez to Hezron
[Am]Hezron to Ram
Ram to Amminadab
[Em]The name remains
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Amminadab father of Nahshon
Nahshon father of Salmon
[Am7]A link in the line of Judah
[Em]A name in the ancient scroll
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
From Perez to Hezron
[G]Hezron to Ram
Ram to [Am7]Amminadab
The name remains
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Jesse and Obed and [Em]Boaz
[Am7]Salah and Nahshon
Ammina[Em]dab and Admin
Ar[Am7]ni and Hezron
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
From Perez [Em]to Hezron
Hezron [Em]to Ram
Ram to Ammi[G]nadab
The name remains
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Am7]Son of Perez
Son of Judah [C]
The line is [Em]clear
{end_of_verse}
